From: Maulik Shah <maulik.shah@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:55:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: Add support for system-suspend-only states

Some domain idle states require system-wide coordination and should not
be selected during regular CPU idle. They remain valid for system-wide
suspend, including s2idle.

Add a per-state system_state boolean and populate it from the
system-state property. The runtime genpd governors skip these states.
genpd_sync_power_off() still uses the system-suspend governor, which is
unchanged, so s2idle can select them.

[omarchy: v2 as posted. genpd_parse_state() in 7.3 ignores a missing
idle-state-name, so the new property read sits next to that call
instead of the error check in the posted context.]

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20261113-s2idle_state-v2-2-ad604182e7e7@oss.qualcomm.com/
Signed-off-by: Maulik Shah <maulik.shah@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/core.c b/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/core.c
@@ -3583,6 +3583,8 @@
 	if (!err)
 		genpd_state->residency_ns = 1000LL * residency;
 
+	genpd_state->system_state = of_property_read_bool(state_node, "system-state");
+
 	of_property_read_string(state_node, "idle-state-name", &genpd_state->name);
 
 	genpd_state->power_on_latency_ns = 1000LL * exit_latency;
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c b/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/governor.c
@@ -183,6 +183,9 @@
 	s64 min_off_time_ns;
 	s64 off_on_time_ns;
 
+	if (genpd->states[state].system_state)
+		return false;
+
 	off_on_time_ns = genpd->states[state].power_off_latency_ns +
 		genpd->states[state].power_on_latency_ns;
 
@@ -405,6 +408,9 @@
 	 */
 	i = genpd->state_idx;
 	do {
+		if (genpd->states[i].system_state)
+			continue;
+
 		if ((idle_duration_ns >= (genpd->states[i].residency_ns +
 		    genpd->states[i].power_off_latency_ns)) &&
 		    (global_constraint >= (genpd->states[i].power_on_latency_ns +
diff --git a/include/linux/pm_domain.h b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
--- a/include/linux/pm_domain.h
+++ b/include/linux/pm_domain.h
@@ -179,6 +179,7 @@
 	s64 power_off_latency_ns;
 	s64 power_on_latency_ns;
 	s64 residency_ns;
+	bool system_state;
 	u64 usage;
 	u64 rejected;
 	u64 above;
